<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent liftings fell in week to Oct 15.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent liftings fell in week to Oct 15.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent crude from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal fell to 686,883 tonnes in the week to October 15, down from 691,242 tonnes the previous week, the Shetland Islands Council Marine Operations Department said.</p>
<p>All but one of the cargoes were destined for refineries in Europe. One cargo of 132,886 tonnes went to Canada.</p>
<p>Below is a list of loadings,  </p>
<p> DATE	    VESSEL		DESTINATION	CARGO (TONNES)</p>
<p>  9/10	   Knock An	    Canaport	   132,886</p>
<p> 10/10	   Westminster	 Pembroke	    81,535</p>
<p> 11/10	   Alandia Prince    Tranmere	    69,299</p>
<p> 12/10	   Alandia Nord	Brunsbuttel	 75,552</p>
<p> 13/10	   Centaur	     Tranmere	    75,716</p>
<p> 13/10	   Berge Septimus    Lavera	     251,895</p>
<p> WK ENDING    U.K.     NWE	AMERICAS    MED    OTHER   TOTAL</p>
<p> 15/10	 226,550  75,552     132,886   251,895  --   686,883</p>
<p>  8/10	 143,192 409,437     138,613     --     --   691,242</p>
<p>  1/10	 147,502 405,988     248,252     --     --   801,742</p>
<p>  24/9	 230,764 138,431     131,800     --     --   500,995</p>
<p>  17/9	 397,164 234,892     372,149     --     -- 1,004,205</p>
